      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the message say what fails without this patch? As far as I can see, a partial range doesn\u0027t lose data at the parent: folio_mapcount() counts slice PTEs, so the dirty/swap-cache check (`folio_mapcount() !\u003d folio_nr_pages()`, 4 !\u003d 1) already skips a folio mapped by several slices, and for a clean folio try_to_unmap_one() puts the PTE back and sets `PG_swapbacked` again as soon as it meets an uncovered dirty slice.\n\nI think what changes is that a fully covered dirty or swap-cache folio can now be freed (the parent always skipped it), and a partly covered clean folio is no longer marked lazyfree and counted in `LazyFree`, which madvise_free_p3s.c in aosp/4367986 checks.",
