      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m worried this stops MADV_FREE from freeing most small folios in 4KB processes, much like the MADV_COLD/MADV_PAGEOUT case on aosp/4367604. do_anonymous_page() maps only the faulting slice and p3s_anon_reuse_sibling_slice() adds the others as they fault, so a folio is mapped by just the slices the process touched, and a window clipped by the VMA never has four. For example, after writing the first two 4KB pages of a 16KB block, `madvise(block, 16K, MADV_FREE)` gets `nr \u003d\u003d 2` here and skips the folio, while the parent still marked it lazyfree when it was clean.\n\nAgreed that MADV_FREE needs more than COLD/PAGEOUT, but as far as I can see it\u0027s enough that every mapping of the folio is one of the `nr` PTEs being cleared: unmapped slices hold no data, since p3s_anon_folio_zero_slice() clears a slice before it is mapped again. That\u0027s also the rule p3s_folio_slices_in_window() uses for reclaim. Would something like this work for you?\n\n```\nif (!folio_test_large(folio)) {\n\tif (nr !\u003d folio_mapcount(folio))\n\t\tcontinue;\n} else if (nr \u003c folio_nr_ptes) {\n```\n\nThe dirty/swap-cache check below would then compare `folio_mapcount(folio)` with `nr`, which equals `folio_nr_pages()` there for native folios.",
